  "docTitle": "Quick Commerce (Blinkit / Zepto / Instamart) - SDE Prep Dojo",
  "description": "Design 10-minute grocery delivery from dark stores: store-scoped search, inventory kept consistent across the warehouse system, the store and the app, stock reservation, order lifecycle, picker and rider assignment, peak-time prioritisation, payments, and a medicine-delivery variant.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n        <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n          <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"4\">Level 4 - Advanced</span>\n          <span class=\"time\">40 min</span>\n          <span class=\"chip accent\">HLD design</span>\n          <span class=\"chip company\">Swiggy</span><span class=\"chip company\">Flipkart</span><span class=\"chip company\">Zepto</span><span class=\"chip company\">Startup</span>\n        </div>\n        <h1>Quick Commerce (Blinkit / Zepto / Instamart)</h1>\n        <p class=\"lead\">Design an app that delivers milk, chips and phone chargers in 10 minutes. You will learn why search must be scoped to one dark store, how to keep stock numbers honest between the warehouse, the shelf and the app, how to reserve the last packet of milk safely, and how pickers and riders are assigned when the evening rush hits. Plus the medicine-delivery variant asked at a startup.</p>\n      "
  },
